; pre: the scsibench pass on the Kickstart drop-in (boot from
; kickstart_rustscsi.zip with the five test disks, see tools/scsibench/README).
; Units: 0 the system disk, 1 t0 (64 MB), 2 t1-4k (4K sectors), 3 t2-3t (3 TB),
; 4 the empty CD-ROM, 5 t3-fs (256 MB). WRITES UNITS 1-5.
;   Execute SHARED:sbench/pre
; Results: SHARED:sbench/out/pre-*.txt
FailAt 30
MakeDir SHARED:sbench/out >NIL:
Copy SHARED:sbench/vscsitest RAM: QUIET
Copy SHARED:sbench/cu9 RAM: QUIET
Copy SHARED:sbench/test_virtioscsi RAM: QUIET
Protect RAM:vscsitest +rwed QUIET
Protect RAM:cu9 +rwed QUIET
Protect RAM:test_virtioscsi +rwed QUIET
Version virtioscsi.device FULL >SHARED:sbench/out/pre-version.txt
; 1. Every command on every test unit (writes units 1-5).
RAM:vscsitest virtioscsi.device 6 6 1 >SHARED:sbench/out/pre-vscsitest.txt
; 2. The system disk through the drop-in: SYS:Libs read, copied to DH0, read back.
CD SYS:Libs
C:MD5Sum #? >SHARED:sbench/out/pre-libs.md5
CD RAM:
MakeDir DH0:sbench >NIL:
Copy SYS:Libs DH0:sbench ALL QUIET
CD DH0:sbench
C:MD5Sum #? >SHARED:sbench/out/pre-dh0copy.md5
CD RAM:
Delete DH0:sbench ALL QUIET FORCE >NIL:
; 3. The C driver's own suite (with the start-up handshake), units 0 and 1.
RAM:test_virtioscsi >SHARED:sbench/out/pre-csuite.txt
; 4. Child processes reading two units at once, and ones that exit at once.
RAM:cu9 50 0 0 1 2 virtioscsi.device >SHARED:sbench/out/pre-cu9real.txt
RAM:cu9 50 0 99 99 2 virtioscsi.device >SHARED:sbench/out/pre-cu9quiet.txt
; 5. Checked random I/O on units 1-3 (no resets on the drop-in).
RAM:vscsitest TORTURE virtioscsi.device 60 1,2,3 8 >SHARED:sbench/out/pre-torture.txt
Echo "== results"
Search SHARED:sbench/out/pre-vscsitest.txt "tests passed" NONUM
Search SHARED:sbench/out/pre-csuite.txt "finished" NONUM
Search SHARED:sbench/out/pre-cu9real.txt "rounds ok" NONUM
Search SHARED:sbench/out/pre-cu9quiet.txt "rounds ok" NONUM
Search SHARED:sbench/out/pre-torture.txt "torture:" NONUM
Echo "== failures"
Search SHARED:sbench/out/pre-vscsitest.txt "FAIL" NONUM
Search SHARED:sbench/out/pre-torture.txt "FAIL" NONUM
Echo "pre done" >SHARED:sbench/out/pre.done
